  "name": "Song of Fate Season",
  "sourceUrl": "https://honkai-star-rail.fandom.com/wiki/Song_of_Fate_Season",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-07-21T09:24:40.108Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Legend says the Chrysos Heir bard Illia once passed through Janusopolis during Fate Season, casually singing this folk song while riding a dromas."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-bbd19a8d6f8cb8b6"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When the year is young and new, Janus bars their ancient door"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The eldest sister of Fate draws borders true, with chains across the cosmic floor"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "See the lines that split the sky, cleaving future from the past"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "All cast earthly bonds aside, and burn the bridges to their yore"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"When these gates swing wide again, new dawns shall rise once more\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-d3daebef2c07a8f5"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the month of perfect time, Talanton winds the springs of fate"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The second sister of Fate with measures fine, weighs all things both small and great"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "See how dawn and dusk align, day and night in equal weight"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Mortals rise when dawn bells ring, rest when sunset takes its place"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Perfect balance shows us all, nothing's truly small or great\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-52eade3108bbb238"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the drowsiest of days, Oronyx spreads sleepy haze"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The youngest sister of Fate falls like ambrosia flows, muting reason's waking prose"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "See how dim the daylight grows, even the Dawn Device drifts to repose"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Mortals drift in dreamy doze, melancholy softly flows"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Let all rest in gentle peace, till new life brings sweet release\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-721c18548320c9a3"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
